t {:answer/id #uuid "aa8f16f0-8d91-524d-a6aa-056212c928df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513506} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b336a22-ce20-5a6b-8abb-1b2bf6621e0a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513501} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1966c371-f5cd-533a-b50b-c25d3af12bab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513493} {:answer/id #uuid "d9bfc506-73a7-5f1a-ba0d-9902c2dfecd5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513510}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1966c371-f5cd-533a-b50b-c25d3af12bab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513493} :answer-field/id #uuid "898b0ba7-8f94-5f12-937e-3c9e1340d9bd" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513503} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd51f513-13b3-5e2a-a5f4-8ea0cbe8e934" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513508} {:answer/id #uuid "dbdd1d37-ee50-5434-a872-54dbbfadaa60" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513511}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd51f513-13b3-5e2a-a5f4-8ea0cbe8e934" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513508} :answer-field/id #uuid "92d709f6-0f95-59b4-926e-926a1db1de8c" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513505}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "074f460b-629a-557e-9e9d-21172a4b49b6" :question/problem "![](images/47/47e9ad1d37498400ffdc20ec56d90a3e4d629d4f8ac951941c2a8e372cdd41e7.png)\n\nThe curve $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Use the unit-spaced tick marks to locate the listed points. At which of the following points is $f(x)$ continuous?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x=- \\frac{3}{2}$\n- **II.** $x=- \\frac{1}{2}$\n- **III.** $x=\\frac{1}{2}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each point separately.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=- \\frac{3}{2}.$ Since there is a jump at $x=- \\frac{3}{2},$ it is impossible to draw the function in the neighborhood of $x=- \\frac{3}{2}$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=- \\frac{1}{2}.$ Since there is a break at $x=- \\frac{1}{2},$ it is impossible to draw the function in the neighborhood of $x=- \\frac{1}{2}$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=\\frac{1}{2}.$ The graph can be drawn in the neighborhood of $x=\\frac{1}{2}$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\nHence, the correct answer is  \"III only\".\n\n \n\n![](images/4d/4db3d16c1d05cf201e94dcbb7a8e53f82e412aa9d70a72c9766022b5d2d79466.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186513495 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4da50c13-2696-580a-aedc-1db9b42c0734" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513498} {:answer/id #uuid "5726127b-42eb-5208-9bc6-de3b5a702723" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513499}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5726127b-42eb-5208-9bc6-de3b5a702723" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513499} :answer-field/id #uuid "35c3db6c-165a-54e7-83a5-f0703881c30f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513496} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4f6c0ea-5692-5763-9248-dc51a93c1d5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513507} {:answer/id #uuid "ca5aaf54-6af6-506b-8c78-59e9d56de304" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513509}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca5aaf54-6af6-506b-8c78-59e9d56de304" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513509} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b774365-9e16-5513-9162-c8106d2cdf11" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513497} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8373cece-ad67-5510-9904-6f36b4bc8a47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513502} {:answer/id #uuid "8ddf54ed-acd2-5154-9e19-4909dc4d9b78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513504}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8373cece-ad67-5510-9904-6f36b4bc8a47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513502} :answer-field/id #uuid "7322198b-13a2-5330-9550-187f296c4657" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513500}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "304021dc-0557-5932-b360-6e01c0194b41" :question/problem "![](images/14/1449fe787d2263ffd6a0d11450b34425aa4f8b0e4bd4cec0ad3a516b3b85df0c.png)\n\nThe curve $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Use the unit-spaced tick marks to locate the listed points. At which of the following points is $f(x)$ continuous?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $x=- \\frac{9}{2}$\n- **II.** $x=-3$\n- **III.** $x=- \\frac{3}{2}$" :question/worked-solution "Let's consider each point separately.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=- \\frac{9}{2}.$ Because there is a jump at $x=- \\frac{9}{2},$ it is impossible to draw the function in the neighborhood of $x=- \\frac{9}{2}$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-3.$ The graph can be drawn in the neighborhood of $x=-3$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=- \\frac{3}{2}.$ Since there is a break at $x=- \\frac{3}{2},$ it is impossible to draw the function in the neighborhood of $x=- \\frac{3}{2}$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\nHence, the correct answer is: \"II only\"."}] :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Function Is Continuous at a Given Point"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068697 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068549 :question/id #uuid "01bca086-0ed4-5626-a357-e0724685f144" :question/math-academy-id "e-3569" :question/problem "![](images/18/1867a80955ae4b456cbcb011eefed96431f2b12926994942613eb947e55e38c6.png)\n\n \n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true? \n\n- $f(x)$ is defined at $x=2$\n\n- $\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow \\, 2}f(x)$ exists\n\n- $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=2$" :question/worked-solution "By inspecting the graph, we can conclude the following:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $f(2)=2.$\n\n- Statement II is false. From the graph, we can see that the left and right-sided limits are different:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{-}}f(x) & =2, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}f(x) & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,  $\\lim_\\limits{x\\rightarrow \\, 2}f(x)$ does not exist.\n\n- Statement III is false.  The graph of the function breaks at $x=2.$ It's impossible to draw the graph of $f(x)$ without taking our pencil off of the paper. Therefore, $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=2.$\n\nIn conclusion, only statement I is true."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f92e521-e7ab-56ba-8eac-0484b140b1a2" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048943 :topic/math-academy-id 625 :topic/title "Finding the Existence of a Limit Using One-Sided Limits"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051049 :topic/math-academy-id 1814 :topic/title "Infinite Limits from Graphs"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069366 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59a2a5f0-3e42-57b4-bad9-206ee3780f81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438320} {:answer/id #uuid "af0d72cc-9b83-5e65-b119-ed68cb865633" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438321}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "59a2a5f0-3e42-57b4-bad9-206ee3780f81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438320} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf1a4d79-1b8d-5950-8a5e-bfcfed26db16" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439189} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61757e96-29e7-5ad6-b13f-368e70c8d57b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438322} {:answer/id #uuid "b0e26259-4957-5803-9056-827b1a4d22de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438323}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0e26259-4957-5803-9056-827b1a4d22de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438323} :answer-field/id #uuid "2501ee59-3780-5be9-bc55-a5f8dde11fd5" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439190} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7aa1d56f-1dd9-5c6a-9405-26299564144c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438324} {:answer/id #uuid "89ca0c5d-ca91-5313-8b14-509ad40774a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438325}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "89ca0c5d-ca91-5313-8b14-509ad40774a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438325} :answer-field/id #uuid "59f15014-19b5-5e80-ad71-25e49dd00eea" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439191}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "544abde9-c223-5348-b980-33df85581d2d" :question/math-academy-id "q-48042" :question/problem "![](images/8e/8eb53506d9e01d09fe3e072a2c6ed1ade05e1cc185693bdd66b34bdf75797ad9.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true with respect to the function $y=f(x)$ whose graph is plotted above.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{-}}f(x)$ is finite\n- **II.** ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}f(x)$ is finite\n- **III.** $f(x)$  has a discontinuity at $x=2$" :question/worked-solution "By inspecting the graph, we can conclude the following:\n\n- Statement I is false. We get ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{-}}f(x)=-\\infty .$\n\n- Statement II is true. We get ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}f(x)=3.$\n\n- Statement III is true. The function contains a break exactly at $x=2$ and it's impossible to draw its graph without taking our pencil off of the paper."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069367 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1338885-9fa5-56a6-bbde-464a7beff78d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439807} {:answer/id #uuid "c73173bd-c83c-504e-9f9a-d56025e0fdde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439808}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c73173bd-c83c-504e-9f9a-d56025e0fdde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439808} :answer-field/id #uuid "bb748d5b-bb9b-5e8c-884e-a291b4ee024f" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440261} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9689ec4f-c734-5a92-8f3f-3bc8bc7f5697" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439809} {:answer/id #uuid "e4abe095-a9a5-582e-9ac5-95107ec344b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439810}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9689ec4f-c734-5a92-8f3f-3bc8bc7f5697" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439809} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8e06b7f-98e6-5fb5-9ff3-c9f6a2f96bc6" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440262} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6fe5f199-131e-595e-9f80-3a37e7df7a07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439811} {:answer/id #uuid "da339f68-232e-501a-ad3b-79e19df38957" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439812}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6fe5f199-131e-595e-9f80-3a37e7df7a07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439811} :answer-field/id #uuid "77f7cc9d-2122-5ca5-9609-e88412505ba8" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440263}] :question/id #uuid "a302c934-1e7e-57a4-882d-8cd125952f61" :question/math-academy-id "q-48064" :question/problem "![](images/02/0218a1e13a0504b20e802100f9e15877beeb2b565a49fe7cd01cf2a0cf0197ee.png)\n\nThe graph of $y = f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f(x)$ is defined at $x = 2$\n- **II.** $lim_(x → 2)f(x)$ exists\n- **III.** $f(x)$ is continuous at $x = 2$" :question/worked-solution "The filled point at x=2 gives f(2)=1. The left and right limits are 1 and -2, so the two-sided limit does not exist and the function is not continuous there."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186234087 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c85d222d-a0dd-512b-ade9-b7297ab2436e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 175921864398