ion/math-academy-id "q-48063" :question/problem "![](images/f5/f5ba5f7cc2ea5aaf405db1abff7e6f28ed4378ba6a5ec88d73c6861ede1d75de.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f(x)$ is defined at $x=2$\n- **II.** ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{-}}f(x)$ exists\n- **III.** $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=2$" :question/worked-solution "By inspecting the graph, we can conclude the following:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $f(2)=1.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, \n${lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{-}}f(x)=3.$\n\n- Statement III is false. The graph of $f(x)$ breaks at $x=2$,  it's impossible to draw the graph without taking our pencil off of the paper."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240786 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1d178d2-5151-5b2b-bf3b-a33cca78a0c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437342} {:answer/id #uuid "abb6ef8c-182a-5285-988c-d54db91431a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437343}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "abb6ef8c-182a-5285-988c-d54db91431a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437343} :answer-field/id #uuid "41be1f60-3f8e-5182-a74a-4843ff7c332a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438700} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab6c31ae-d701-59ea-a24e-bccbbbef88f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437344} {:answer/id #uuid "ba6eaced-5a92-52d8-8b9f-4552316e18db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437345}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab6c31ae-d701-59ea-a24e-bccbbbef88f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437344} :answer-field/id #uuid "d70122b3-7ecd-576a-83cc-62f210fbd138" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438701} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "502d7dde-403b-5c82-bce4-cc5d707120e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437346} {:answer/id #uuid "43da692e-60dd-5fc5-bc75-f0ee42a60a7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437347}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "502d7dde-403b-5c82-bce4-cc5d707120e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437346} :answer-field/id #uuid "d72ba1c3-2115-5bb6-b6b6-9c5c9cd843d9" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438702}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "340a8e11-ca0d-5e08-ab08-b9647c00e4dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-104049" :question/problem "![](images/51/5143df65d0f99c6511dc8ab13262831669c88535e19c986dacdb364e04847f58.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true with respect to the function $y=f(x)$ whose graph is plotted above.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f(x)$ is defined at $x=2$\n- **II.** ${lim}_{x\\to \\,2}f(x)\\ne f(2)$\n- **III.** $f(x)$ has a discontinuity at $x=2$" :question/worked-solution "By inspecting the graph, we can conclude the following:\n\n- Statement I is true. We have $f(2)=2.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Indeed, from the graph we see that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{-}}f(x) & =2, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}f(x) & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, ${lim}_{x\\to \\,2}f(x)=2=f(2).$\n\n- Statement III is false. The graph of the function doesn't have a break at $x=2$ and we can draw the graph of $f(x)$ around $x=2$ without taking our pencil off of the paper."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240787 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60efdf1c-df12-5856-aa4c-f4f6fc23d42f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437348} {:answer/id #uuid "cea4be79-bc3f-5364-9f0f-d13cc3390e5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437349}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cea4be79-bc3f-5364-9f0f-d13cc3390e5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437349} :answer-field/id #uuid "67208bb7-2119-51cc-97f2-fc43b1d95b36" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438703} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ef42aad5-fee8-5449-bbd4-f1ddf4d65e51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437350} {:answer/id #uuid "7f3c2501-c170-5ad7-8f83-f02c8744f9ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437351}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef42aad5-fee8-5449-bbd4-f1ddf4d65e51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437350} :answer-field/id #uuid "9f1b2ad2-b8cf-5da8-ab38-a32e460f880a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438704} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e135984-0cd0-5f07-bdfa-2c1791ff56da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437352} {:answer/id #uuid "8ac001f4-ce03-575e-80fe-299ba4a5012e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437353}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ac001f4-ce03-575e-80fe-299ba4a5012e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437353} :answer-field/id #uuid "f18fe838-0660-5c6a-8fe2-0675d1705648" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438705}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fc9393f2-809c-5769-b329-186102da51c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-104051" :question/problem "![](images/65/65b9b32e8fac6a71141ce820855058367e9235129de7334db35a200905474cc0.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f(x)$ is defined at $x=5$\n\n- **II.** ${lim}_{x\\to \\,5}f(x)$ exists\n\n- **III.** $f(x)$ has a discontinuity at $x=5$" :question/worked-solution "By inspecting the graph, we can conclude the following:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $f(5)=2.$\n\n- Statement II is false. Indeed, from the graph we see that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{5}^{-}}f(x) & =2, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,{5}^{+}}f(x) & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,  ${lim}_{x\\to \\,5}f(x)$ doesn't exist\n\n- Statement III is true. The graph of the function has a jump exactly at $x=5$\nand it's impossible to draw the graph without taking our pencil off of the paper."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240788 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96e53957-3adf-512d-a153-562190ecd98a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437354} {:answer/id #uuid "be515943-b831-586a-a2a6-0858894c576e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437355}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "be515943-b831-586a-a2a6-0858894c576e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437355} :answer-field/id #uuid "00a7a20b-ccbd-524b-8f79-400afb75fc99" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438706} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d596de00-8611-5fa7-8c45-9ce273f5c8b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437356} {:answer/id #uuid "0966841c-0adf-529b-aba1-cb81f9995b41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437357}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0966841c-0adf-529b-aba1-cb81f9995b41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437357} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca8755ff-7b6f-5f08-b14f-f993ca66343d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438707} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "838f207e-53e0-52c7-92ca-2adcfd316d2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437358} {:answer/id #uuid "17a322fb-de3b-566d-b977-0791a738d3ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437359}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "838f207e-53e0-52c7-92ca-2adcfd316d2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437358} :answer-field/id #uuid "cd33cb2a-e191-5a12-95bb-03979c786429" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438708}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3312f9fe-c2a1-5d75-b752-6c981a0a3f4b" :question/math-academy-id "q-104052" :question/problem "![](images/80/8086893e4587e68f8257b75f2070cf622fa141199d6bd8960f7c4fd8e7bcb349.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f(x)$ is **not** defined at $x=0$\n- **II.** ${lim}_{x\\to \\,0}f(x)$ exists\n- **III.** $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=0$" :question/worked-solution "By inspecting the graph, we can conclude the following:\n\n- Statement I is true. From the graph we can see that no value has been assigned to $f(x)$ at $x=0.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{-}}f(x) & =3, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,{0}^{+}}f(x) & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n${lim}_{x\\to \\,0}f(x)=3.$\n\n- Statement III is false. The function is not even defined at $x=0.$ The graph contains a break at $x=0.$ It's impossible to draw the graph of $f(x)$ without taking our pencil off of the paper."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186240800 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9a2f64f-b3f7-5269-98a9-f17f1936fd6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437360} {:answer/id #uuid "5aba2d92-17d5-581b-ba83-416e31577135" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437361}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9a2f64f-b3f7-5269-98a9-f17f1936fd6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437360} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4034323-df06-5913-aef3-95acdc3329f0" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438709} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd2e9d86-8a7c-5cbe-b475-279c1ac2a7a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437362} {:answer/id #uuid "93a98b73-c51c-50d7-a355-1c0058c19b7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437363}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93a98b73-c51c-50d7-a355-1c0058c19b7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437363} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4dd43e3-cfa3-5d79-a551-739b688c4abe" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438710} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c70f8b35-be7c-5f76-ad36-eb2923e9983e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437364} {:answer/id #uuid "1ce5ebea-8788-5a88-b6b5-adf0418527ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437365}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ce5ebea-8788-5a88-b6b5-adf0418527ff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186437365} :answer-field/id #uuid "470e2c3a-d1de-5b69-b0fa-560f0d53fa11" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438711}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ad98348d-cbe6-535a-9828-f9008c2ec2e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-104124" :question/problem "![](images/bd/bdcfa35fb04028cbff32992b41214c878443d3815b676a0cf046f5a99bd771bd.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f(x)$ is **not** defined at $x=-2$\n- **II.** ${lim}_{x\\to \\,-2}f(x)=f(-2)$\n- **III.** $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-2$" :question/worked-solution "By inspecting the graph, we can conclude the following:\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, $f(x)$ is defined at $x=-2$ and $f(-2)=5.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, from the graph we see that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,-{2}^{-}}f(x) & =5, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,-{2}^{+}}f(x) & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, ${lim}_{x\\to \\,-2}f(x)=5=f(-2).$\n\n- Statement III is true. The graph of $f(x)$ can be drawn without taking our pencil off of the paper in the neighborhood of $x=-2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329853 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a72f0e3-10f9-5627-abc6-e3f1fa8f8634" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438314} {:answer/id #uuid "e39e9c9e-b76e-54bc-917d-488397305de1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438315}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e39e9c9e-b76e-54bc-917d-488397305de1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438315} :answer-field/id #uuid "d07a11c2-3a82-577e-86eb-fdf2c8fb7f18" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439186} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a260fa98-0877-521e-9d9f-d5b6a870fdd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438316} {:answer/id #uuid "1bc1372a-793e-581e-ba95-60ccf10a257d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438317}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a260fa98-0877-521e-9d9f-d5b6a870fdd6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438316} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4d5181e-ff19-543a-8abc-820b23948742" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439187} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5ddcb0bf-22bc-580a-9f9f-9c09ea70ffbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438318} {:answer/id #uuid "b8110f84-150f-541f-b756-551b0e23ad1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438319}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ddcb0bf-22bc-580a-9f9f-9c09ea70ffbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438318} :answer-field/id #uuid "33037cbe-1756-5c5e-b354-7c66976c18f6" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439188}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "18223e97-17ad-509c-a688-bf8d869b747a" :question/math-academy-id "q-48040" :question/problem "![](images/59/59c02273515e87fcebb8eb1785dc2cf0c6490feda4fc9644df43b8849921eec5.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f(x)$ is defined at $x=-1$\n- **II.** ${lim}_{x\\to \\,-1}f(x)$ exists\n- **III.** $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-1$" :question/worked-solution "By inspecting the graph, we can conclude the following:\n\n- Statement I is true. The function $f(x)$ is defined at $x=-1$ and we have $f(-1)=1.$\n\n- Statement II is false. We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,-{1}^{-}}f(x) & =2, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,-{1}^{+}}f(x) & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, both left-hand side and right-hand side limits exist but they are not the same. Therefore, ${lim}_{x\\to \\,-1}f(x)$ does not exist.\n\n- Statement III is false. The function contains a break exactly at $x=-1$ and it's impossible to draw its graph without taking our pencil off of the paper."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329854 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e385f975-d87c-58b3-b71c-b590f2934163" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438326} {:answer/id #uuid "ef8e886b-57f2-59c5-b759-e8c984922226" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438327}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e385f975-d87c-58b3-b71c-b590f2934163" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438326} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae70a57b-88e6-5264-9484-75fdbfb3d260" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439192} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c504c9e2-a62c-527b-a9e7-002c0a5d6492" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438328} {:answer/id #uuid "f1d2fa27-53f5-5bde-85b6-c4f96e3a4c65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438329}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f1d2fa27-53f5-5bde-85b6-c4f96e3a4c65" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438329} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ed00390-f87b-59cf-b29a-87e97f2baa99" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439193} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bd6d307-6b90-5d32-8396-2192f0a65d3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438330} {:answer/id #uuid "278fac04-a440-5c31-bf6f-e56fa749884f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438331}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1bd6d307-6b90-5d32-8396-2192f0a65d3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438330} :answer-field/id #uuid "4150e66a-c62a-5f54-84bd-4cbabf0439eb" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439194}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "96069899-bca3-51de-b64c-6e29072ea13e" :question/math-academy-id "q-48062" :question/problem "![](images/d9/d9db7f2a491ae3065dbe8434a71d378c4fed8fec16c82e2fd76dcb209c786809.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f(x)$ is defined at $x=1$\n\n- **II.** ${lim}_{x\\to \\,1}f(x)$ exists\n\n- **III.** $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=1$" :question/worked-solution "By inspecting the graph, we can conclude the following:\n\n- Statement I is false. From the graph we can see that no value has been assigned to $f(x)$ at $x=1.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{-}}f(x) & =1, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{+}}f(x) & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, \n${lim}_{x\\to \\,1}f(x)=1.$\n\n- Statement III is false. The function is not even defined at $x=1.$ The graph contains a break at $x=1.$ It's impossible to draw the graph of $f(x)$ without taking our pencil off of the paper."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329855 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cea1630d-9468-583c-91a2-a690bea97b38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438332} {:a