-academy-id "q-48065" :question/problem "![](images/fa/fa15192923f9fd7370818fcb6b05b24b3bb6901dfbf90dd53539d71fd0f8b0bf.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $f(x)$ is defined at $x=2$\n\n- **II.** ${lim}_{x\\to \\,2}f(x)=f(2)$\n\n- **III.** $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=2$" :question/worked-solution "By inspecting the graph, we can conclude the following:\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, $f(x)$ is defined at $x=2$ and $f(2)=1.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, from the graph we see that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{-}}f(x) & =1, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,{2}^{+}}f(x) & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, ${lim}_{x\\to \\,2}f(x)=1=f(2).$\n\n- Statement III is true. The graph of $f(x)$ can be drawn without taking our pencil off of the paper in the neighborhood of $x=2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329856 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e4df05ec-0fe6-54f0-8bc1-cf5538337e0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438338} {:answer/id #uuid "9b5a2e77-1669-5312-ba49-6c3d96d17708" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438339}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b5a2e77-1669-5312-ba49-6c3d96d17708" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438339} :answer-field/id #uuid "43790721-2fa7-55ee-a69d-a64086e46f6b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439198} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9084bea7-0a1c-5582-8861-25e25b0d0500" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438340} {:answer/id #uuid "020fea39-bd88-5bcc-be48-cde9e74cef5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438341}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "020fea39-b