/ref 17592186329857 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "482eccea-2346-5593-868b-442a966e9a8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438344} {:answer/id #uuid "8b899347-5cdc-55eb-9237-340f14f06adc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438345}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b899347-5cdc-55eb-9237-340f14f06adc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438345} :answer-field/id #uuid "b283e793-d4da-5d69-a5a1-be0029df36aa" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439201} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "eedcb44f-6a3f-5120-9c70-1dd58a08e127" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438346} {:answer/id #uuid "d13de6d5-bfdc-5c50-a6df-fb0dcbf26655" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438347}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eedcb44f-6a3f-5120-9c70-1dd58a08e127" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438346} :answer-field/id #uuid "5abdce64-f6f6-52a3-8cab-3d32c79d7f41" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439202} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c53815f-dbbf-597d-bc77-e3c95eb214a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438348} {:answer/id #uuid "9d4a1be4-1771-5700-ad05-4ae3a028b5b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438349}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d4a1be4-1771-5700-ad05-4ae3a028b5b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186438349} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b5b96a8-998c-5f10-bb84-99eac175deab" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439203}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f506060c-db8a-5e26-aad7-74b6b6b44f61" :question/math-academy-id "q-48068" :question/problem "![](images/8a/8a3874b7907227653d93451d9ce0960fdadc8cb3e10396e0f27f7ebb363bebe2.png)\n\nWhich of the following statements are true with respect to the function $y=f(x)$ whose graph is plotted above.\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{-}}f(x)$ is finite\n- **II.** ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{+}}f(x)$ is **not** finite\n- **III.** $f(x)$  is  continuous at $x=-1$" :question/worked-solution "By inspecting the graph, we can conclude the following:\n\n- Statement I is true. We get ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{-}}f(x)=1.$\n\n- Statement II is false. We get ${lim}_{x\\to \\,{1}^{+}}f(x)=1.$\n\n- Statement III is true. The graph of the function doesn't have a break at $x=-1$ and we can draw the graph of $f(x)$ around $x=-1$ without taking our pencil off of the paper."}] :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Behavior of a Function in the Neighborhood of a Point"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096701 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096495 :question/id #uuid "839ed5f5-165f-5de5-aba1-551ac605475f" :question/math-academy-id "e-5212" :question/problem "Consider the picture below.\n\n![](images/f2/f2518c2e998e7c7f551548a4cc7283720a66428ea8fa9872494a81cc3848ba9e.png)\n\nGiven that ![](images/c6/c6714d0a6eaa5c7d354d46e8d6d60da7f3d2011df0fc75773036cf7ae510c5e3.png), find ![](images/24/24878591902884f45f14f5c447bc326586a411a8870b205fc12825a4ab2c738a.png)" :question/worked-solution "Recall that when two known vectors are not parallel, a linear combination of them is unique. So, once we rewrite ![](images/5c/5c644b15efcf5a4274de23242a722604ead2ff800ea29ba7a650729227fefdf0.png) in terms of ![](images/27/27f36b1d1846e12e3c50b7d4e47f5745727792d52a48e4d85b689ec36e3d25a0.png) and ![](images/a7/a7b9033c421072576aaf959980d778c319a8ed0f849e08db644b63bc6994088c.png) we can match coefficients to determine the unknown scalar.\n\nTo find ![](images/16/166c90a9c29f99347bff6b397f31d705ec6407a19b4d71246f98308bbd7a5473.png) we want to match the expression\n![](images/fc/fc79367916dd7671c17de4f40b3d83f91d41c2f9988645964de0b53e5b11ab9b.png)\n\nWe are given that one of the components is ![](images/91/91f686c6ca02e85c386cb0f9e80b66beface446d3a541952e0ac91738ad0db37.png) So, we first draw the vector ![](images/d5/d54b9a8919c7b6106fcf5770c62b1823605d7be98a55d5333e73bcfb7528997a.png) from the origin. Then we complete the path to the point ![](images/6e/6e1bbbe9eb66856824ff70d16cc2c077519d361546b226a67146e20f15a24dd0.png)\n\n![](images/ea/ea517ac4ca8e0bcf7ba48f23e66f100323d5485f1221219aacfbea9148f4a1af.png)\n\nNote that in ![](images/f1/f1c944e6afa4e9cd84bc68004a2bfd918d81498a727aeb7c56ec627806bf93f6.png), we have:\n\n- ![](images/b7/b7ac390c4e43b2fa2fbb4063632f98869256cea877caa5e5dad4aad33ae94722.png)\n\n- ![](images/7e/7e5f2b01647ab01052fff18ab760273eebe19d47b56051b1953adf587d7f9fb3.png) and ![](images/78/784225d11bf94b7fbd67f8e2395695141eb75b1cb44f89d49b29bb3a2031534b.png) have the same direction\n\nHence, ![](images/21/21261c8ad0d86a9e7300ffc58c57fd76beef9f627492bcfe2051d5e3cfd82a4e.png)\n\nAdditionally,\n![](images/ae/ae9c98ded3aa4317a729571710ad38d973a2d67b5faeb9ad26af7c24ee5c3193.png)\n\nConsequently, ![](images/ae/aee3287ad64a654880216142756811bd4d5232b3dba2f48378b8b1c5241e4316.png)\n\nSince ![](images/46/466863f8c7522ac89896a4233a823be02940535097c28328fa2c9e9e1f4bc3d8.png) the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of ![](images/37/3720c5887713d3f7a29be384fe5e883390935b2b9b469af626a8dba968f4da8b.png) we get:\n![](images/4a/4ac145b710c5354b44a4ea1dc820d70f54b5c17985f078fce6313b671ec26fd9.png)"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2fbb8f19-f35a-59c4-9b77-8f6c3542ef28" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050467 :topic/math-academy-id 1102 :topic/title "Problem Solving Using Vector Diagrams"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186051014 :topic/math-academy-id 1105 :topic/title "Linear Combinations of Vectors and Their Properties"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097164 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00092400-4bdb-54aa-b9f7-3bbc79220342" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284786} {:answer/id #uuid "132972e0-7a7c-5c06-9851-0cd678b28702" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284957} {:answer/id #uuid "159ed092-bb37-575a-9d11-ee33122bcff6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284980} {:answer/id #uuid "4c63c7e5-c9c3-51e0-9d4a-a4807711e12e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285498} {:answer/id #uuid "caceb281-75a2-5c25-ace0-e5023bde2a8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286636}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "159ed092-bb37-575a-9d11-ee33122bcff6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284980} :answer-field/id #uuid "518cd3fd-d07a-569f-9cb4-9c2cf6e0f0c2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287328}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "767cbe5b-8f45-54bf-8422-666ebc7778f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-19338" :question/problem "![](images/81/816c4ecbfe49321bc6b2bc0d72eb61d6ddd1aeae7e76a275df0975439dde5865.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Given that $c=a+\\lambda b,$ find $\\lambda .$" :question/worked-solution "To find $\\lambda ,$ we want to match the expression\n\n$$\nc=a+\\lambda b.\n$$\n\nWe are given that one of the components is $a.$ So, we begin with the vector $a,$ and then find the remaining vector needed to reach the point $C.$\n\n![](images/67/6782f2fa59056afd9022edbaf69c44a991bf12a7ac6a190bea3cc08fc7a4996c.png)\n\nNote that in $△OAC,$ we have:\n\n- $AC=2.5|b|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $b$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}=2.5b.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{AC} \\\\  & =a+2.5b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $c=a+\\lambda b=a+2.5b.$\n\nSince $a∦b,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of $b,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\lambda =2.5\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097181 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2cc5590c-f5cf-5e21-9a2e-5e31772b304d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285183} {:answer/id #uuid "35a20bbd-e86d-5f6e-907f-c57e5562aefc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285280} {:answer/id #uuid "531f071e-da47-5a18-876a-8d7ce3863d67" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285552} {:answer/id #uuid "80ddc038-3db7-5447-8486-3d32260a66f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285973} {:answer/id #uuid "b9a429df-36c3-50d3-a2b3-d9bf1a44b2dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286477}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9a429df-36c3-50d3-a2b3-d9bf1a44b2dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286477} :answer-field/id #uuid "7fd9a91d-854c-5377-a157-19bd44fd94f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287416}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7a4f66a0-1cfd-52d9-be40-ea47c3b77cf3" :question/math-academy-id "q-20435" :question/problem "![](images/4b/4b7c8c679171c1dcb6ef44b33696ba2ccce87b3f690643af979476d8dfb285ce.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Given that $c=\\lambda a+3b$, find $\\lambda .$" :question/worked-solution "To find $\\lambda ,$ we want to match the expression\n\n$$\nc=\\lambda a+3b.\n$$\n\nWe are given that one of the components is $3b.$ So, we first draw the vector $3b$ from the origin. Then we complete the path to the point $C.$\n\n![](images/f6/f67af4512a7ab61f862932a60dafc25ef62bc46335b7d7df323fe889f8728e6b.png)\n\nLet $P$ be the endpoint of the vector $3b.$ Then\n\n$$\nc=\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC}.\n$$\n\nIn $△OPC,$ we have:\n\n- $PC=\\frac{1}{2}|a|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{PC}$ and $a$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{PC}=\\frac{1}{2}a.$\n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC} \\\\  & =3b+\\frac{1}{2}a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $c=\\lambda a+3b=\\frac{1}{2}a+3b.$\n\nSince $a∦b,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of $a,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\lambda =\\frac{1}{2}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256370 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f58b1f0-a1f2-5152-8b50-a3b88cfa03ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253806} {:answer/id #uuid "28d1e0c0-6ce0-5a30-b308-d0185860ae28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254035} {:answer/id #uuid "86b0f05f-4928-50e1-9fee-05c5f1c722c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254862} {:answer/id #uuid "c1aa28fa-00bb-55da-83ba-fd94389b454c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255398} {:answer/id #uuid "f72b66ba-7fc3-5027-b7a4-6cc62030c64e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255836}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0f58b1f0-a1f2-5152-8b50-a3b88cfa03ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253806} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bffb12d-46cf-5b60-8dd5-5eb835abe4b0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255967}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "701d4729-670a-58df-8c65-907d28621390" :question/math-academy-id "q-120244" :question/problem "![](images/9e/9e595809380e3067934b9f8c86933dd5300fcfb54ce4202eddc0e4196b74cf00.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Given that $c=a+\\lambda b,$ find $\\lambda .$" :question/worked-solution "To find $\\lambda ,$ we want to match the expression\n\n$$\nc=a+\\lambda b.\n$$\n\nWe are given that one of the components is $a.$ So, we begin with the vector $a,$ and then find the remaining vector needed to reach the point $C.$\n\n![](images/0c/0c785e189beebb0a803bceba272db156af6d3b47c690ee9527876f77c65d1891.png)\n\nNote that in $△OAC,$ we have:\n\n- $AC=2|b|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $b$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}=2b.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{AC} \\\\  & =a+2b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $c=a+\\lambda b=a+2b.$\n\nSince $a∦b,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of $b,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\lambda =2\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186256371 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0335560b-a354-5aa4-b231-eab70eea8ddf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253694} {:answer/id #uuid "1e21b15d-d740-5a5b-9c81-a80ec1a76c3e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253923} {:answer/id #uuid "3400ad14-ce2a-5d97-b3ef-9cad4db20aff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254119} {:answer/id #uuid "9588a3fa-37df-5403-bcd0-6fe653faf445" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254987} {:answer/id #uuid "b9e8937f-908d-5315-adb1-a5131958d010" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186255328}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3400ad14-ce2a-5d97-b3ef-9cad4db20aff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186254119} :answer-field/id #uuid "73b1acee-2901-571f-8ea9-fb67bf575d10" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256132}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5bdd11f1-936c-5b1f-8197-4ca4897841c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-120245" :question/problem "![](images/58/58901401bfe81e040e22da6e07d543423db58a845009a80525eae131752874d4.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Given that $c=\\lambda a+3b$, find $\\lambda .$" :question/worked-solution "To find $\\lambda ,$ we want to match the expression\n\n$$\nc=\\lambda a+3b.\n$$\n\nWe are given that one of the components is $3b.$ So, we first draw the vector $3b$ from the origin. Then we complete the path to the point $C.$\n\n![](images/3e/3effb654f4db5e1f207c671116baf648cb70f90781882a1fd758f32b610aefca.png)\n\nLet $P$ be the endpoint of the vector $3b.$ Then\n\n$$\nc=\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC}.\n$$\n\nIn $△OPC,$ we have:\n\n- $PC=2|a|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{PC}$ and $a$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{PC}=2a.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC} \\\\  & =3b+2a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $c=\\lambda a+3b=2a+3b.$\n\nSince $a∦b,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of $a,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\lambda =2\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292806 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c882697d-3ff6-59d8-b2c0-0350fa54d637" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291493}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c882697d-3ff6-59d8-b2c0-0350fa54d637" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291493} :answer-field/id #uuid "969d3969-f0db-5103-b554-1385312b25f5" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292210}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ea485cdb-41da-5e4e-87b0-f133e79c3191" :question/math-academy-id "q-275120" :question/problem "![](images/1d/1d637a841739052b4e2d26f89bbcfd92eefefcebf6000a46a10a45b7e53ecf15.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. If $c=\\lambda a+3b,$ then$\\,\\lambda =$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find $\\lambda ,$ we want to match the expression\n\n$$\nc=\\lambda a+3b.\n$$\n\nWe are given that one of the components is $3b.$ So, we first draw the vector $3b$ from the origin. Then we complete the path to the point $C.$\n\n![](images/33/33a5661bc10830c7e52e2ba7f27779a28c6e5f9cf39630e60d0634f3b6f7ccdd.png)\n\nLet $P$ be the endpoint of the vector $3b.$ Then\n\n$$\nc=\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC}.\n$$\n\nIn $△OPC,$ we have:\n\n- $PC=3|a|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{PC}$ and $a$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{PC}=3a.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC} \\\\  & =3b+3a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $c=\\lambda a+3b=3a+3b.$\n\nSince $a∦b,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of $a,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\lambda =3.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302041 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee03130e-7005-5beb-9b84-a33367f0c7bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2/3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301139}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee03130e-7005-5beb-9b84-a33367f0c7bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2/3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301139} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9b6b305-fb35-5362-91ad-13c85e2a65c2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301773}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "17bceb35-b5fb-536b-bf3f-edb50187b769" :question/math-academy-id "q-321299" :question/problem "![](images/6f/6fe3721ff3ab63e75be934c79b03d4ca601513c2e08b987a0bafd94c74856e90.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. If $c=a+\\lambda b$, then$\\,\\lambda =$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find $\\lambda ,$ we want to match the expression\n\n$$\nc=a+\\lambda b.\n$$\n\nWe are given that one of the components is $a.$ So, we begin with the vector $a,$ and then find the remaining vector needed to reach the point $C.$\n\n![](images/9c/9c8d67718152bc1bc9569213369580b6fc6f5bc1fe0c63b637f14c9f659dfe27.png)\n\nNote that in $△OAC,$ we have:\n\n- $AC=\\frac{2}{3}|b|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ and $b$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{AC}=\\frac{2}{3}b.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{AC} \\\\  & =a+\\frac{2}{3}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $c=a+\\lambda b=a+\\frac{2}{3}b.$\n\nSince $a∦b,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of $b,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\lambda =\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302311 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f77b9a46-e79c-5237-bc79-ede8d68a69b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301182}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f77b9a46-e79c-5237-bc79-ede8d68a69b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301182} :answer-field/id #uuid "5972d618-ef56-509e-bacd-8caba67f5cfd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301522}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident 