b,$ then$\\,\\lambda =$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find $\\lambda ,$ we want to match the expression\n\n$$\nc=\\lambda a+2b.\n$$\n\nWe are given that one of the components is $2b.$ So, we first draw the vector $2b$ from the origin. Then we complete the path to the point $C.$\n\n![](images/1d/1d266a8324d18191f5bc8560be6539d54d1a11916f33ead7432d9f528769fc22.png)\n\nLet $P$ be the endpoint of the vector $2b.$ Then\n\n$$\nc=\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC}.\n$$\n\nIn $△OPC,$ we have:\n\n- $PC=\\frac{1}{2}|a|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{PC}$ and $a$ have the same direction\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{PC}=\\frac{1}{2}a.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC} \\\\  & =2b+\\frac{1}{2}a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $c=\\lambda a+2b=\\frac{1}{2}a+2b.$\n\nSince $a∦b,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of $a,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\lambda =\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338753 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4416194-05a6-5e46-bc9c-4c7b0b05b834" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337775} {:answer/id #uuid "d97d4b30-65f6-5e94-8ced-509f035a553f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186337924} {:answer/id #uuid "ea12c352-cf2e-574d-8e8b-85bb3bd14e46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338074} {:answer/id #uuid "eecb979e-b097-506c-b7e4-d9bb4c85501e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338120} {:answer/id #uuid "ef332865-a8b3-594f-849a-8f281bcf7db5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338124}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea12c352-cf2e-574d-8e8b-85bb3bd14e46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338074} :answer-f